cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Green City Map or its city data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Green City Map"
abstract: >-
  An AI agent skill that scores every residential street of a city from 0 to 100
  for how good it is to live on: light and open views, trees and green, nature on
  foot, quiet, few tourists, and daily needs without a car. It uses open data only
  (OpenStreetMap, Overture Maps, Copernicus Sentinel-2, ESA WorldCover). The code is
  under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0; the city data it makes is under
  the Open Database License 1.0.
authors:
  - alias: broAir
repository-code: "https://github.com/broAir/green-city-map"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
version: "0.2.0"
keywords:
  - street livability
  - walkability
  - green space
  - urban noise
  - tourism
  - OpenStreetMap
  - Overture Maps
  - Sentinel-2
  - open data
  - AI agent skill
